join durai left
join oleysa right

oleysa: Good evening, Durai.
durai: God, is it that late already? I'm not super eager to get out there. I don't know if I can really, "perform", in this cold weather...
oleysa: You have a 2 inch thick mascot costume. You'll be fine.
Durai exits
durai: OH, HELLO YOUNG MAN! GEE, YOUR CLOTHES LOOK DIRTY! WHY NOT COME IN AND BUY SOME LAUNDRY DETERGENT?
durai: AH, SOME GENTLEMEN ON A NIGHT OUT! I KNOW ALL ABOUT NIGHTS OUT - MY FAMILY, BACK IN SAVINGSLAND, USED TO -
durai: SIR, THAT'S JUST NOT A VERY NICE THING TO SAY. YEAH OF COURSE YOU FIND IT FUNNY.
durai: UM, YOU THERE, MA'AM! PERHAPS YOU'RE OUT LATE TO GO SEE A MOVIE? WHY NOT COME IN AND BUY SOME POPCORN... UM, OKAY!
Durai enters
durai: I don't think anyone liked my act today.
oleysa: Well, you need to understand, Durai, that people who walk around in the dark are pretty different to your usual crowd.
durai: Oh, do you think I should, like... change tack?
oleysa: Yes. These night people...
oleysa: Our usual clientele, very organized. They zip in, pick up something, and leave. They have somewhere to be.
oleysa: Night people generally just waste their own time. Walking around, running a Buck's party, doing a nightclub, making a graffiti.
oleysa: They're all kind of... stupid. So kind of just make it clear what we can offer them, and they'll flock to us like flies.
durai: What can we offer them?
oleysa: Oh, what do they like... Cheap beer. Coffee. Horrible food.
durai: Ah! Okay. Loud and clear.
Durai exits
durai: NEED SOME HORRIBLE FOOD? HEAD RIGHT THIS WAY! OUR BEER AND COFFEE MIX IS AS CHEAP AS COULD BE!
oleysa: Durai, no-
customeroy: Hey, we heard about a beer and coffee cocktail. How much for a party of 5?
oleysa: ...?
oleysa: Um, let me just... mix it. Now.
oleysa: ...
oleysa: Now, the cocktail is done. It will cost, four...teen. Pounds.
customeroy: Thanks, lady. Very punk.
game: Durai's improvised cocktail really moved sales. Good shift.
[signal arg="shift_good"]